description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/activity-lifecycle-audit.ts, insert one block into the traceTimestamp function.

The file contains this exact block:

  if (typeof t.started_at === "string") {
    const v = Date.parse(t.started_at);
    if (!Number.isNaN(v)) return v;
  }

Immediately after it, insert exactly:

  const ex = (t as { executed_at?: unknown }).executed_at;
  if (typeof ex === "string") {
    const w = Date.parse(ex);
    if (!Number.isNaN(w)) return w;
  }

Insert only. Do not modify any other line, interface, or function.

Facts, each stated positively:
1. Every trace row passed to traceTimestamp carries executed_at as an ISO date string, for example "2026-09-04T10:53:30.299061668Z".
2. The guard `typeof ex === "string"` is the populated-check; Date.parse runs only when that guard is true.
3. traceTimestamp's return value is read at line 240 of this file and assigned into bucket.newest, which sets recency and therefore combined_score.
4. This block is reached whenever the earlier guards fall through, which is the normal case.

